# What never enters the image build context (Containerfile). The repo root
# holds multi-hundred-MB server logs and a Windows `target/`, so this file is
# the difference between a two-second context upload and a ten-minute one.

# Build outputs. kernel/build especially: it carries a CMakeCache.txt written
# by the MSVC generator, and cmake refuses to reconfigure someone else's cache
# in the container ("CMakeCache.txt directory is different").
#
# Spelled out rather than `kernel/build*/`: an ignore pattern's trailing slash
# is dropped before matching, so that glob also swallows kernel/build.sh --
# the script the Linux build.rs runs -- and the failure is a `bash: No such
# file or directory` an hour into the image build.
target/
kernel/build
kernel/build-*
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vitest/
node_modules/

# What CI writes back into the repo root from this same Containerfile. The
# release job exports the `artifacts` stage to `out/linux` and then packages
# it as `ignis-v<version>-<triple>/`, both inside the build context -- so
# without these the image build that follows sees a different `COPY . .` than
# the artifacts build did, misses the cache on it, and recompiles the whole
# workspace a second time (measured: 429s of a 610s step).
out/
ignis-v*/
ignis-v*.tar.gz*
ignis-v*.zip*

# Logs (ignis-server.log alone is ~270 MB) and profiler captures, which embed
# the profiled process's environment.
*.log
*.log.err
_bench_logs/
*.nsys-rep
*.nsys-rep.sqlite
*.qdrep

# The artifact store is a symlink to a path outside the repo; it resolves to
# nothing in the build context, and the model is mounted at runtime anyway.
models

# Scratch, local state and recorded traces.
.scratch/
.git/
.github/
.qwen/
.claude/
.codex/
local.mk
bench/traces/*.jsonl
__pycache__/
*.pyc
